# Metro Station Finder 2025 - Cursor Rules
# Modern, Blazing Fast, Type-Safe Development Standards

## 🎯 Project Goals
- Blazing fast performance (sub-second page loads)
- Modern, accessible UI with dark mode
- Type-safe throughout
- Zero runtime errors
- Exceptional developer experience

## 🏗️ Architecture Standards

### Next.js 15 App Router
- ALWAYS use App Router, never Pages Router
- Prefer Server Components over Client Components
- Use "use client" directive sparingly and at the lowest possible level
- Leverage React 19 Server Actions for mutations
- Use Suspense boundaries for loading states
- Implement streaming for better UX

### File Structure & Organization
```
src/
├── app/                    # App Router pages
│   ├── (auth)/            # Route groups for auth pages
│   ├── (dashboard)/       # Route groups for dashboard
│   ├── globals.css        # Global styles
│   ├── layout.tsx         # Root layout
│   └── page.tsx           # Home page
├── components/            # Reusable components
│   ├── ui/               # Shadcn/ui base components
│   ├── custom/           # Custom components
│   └── layout/           # Layout components
├── lib/                  # Utilities and configurations
│   ├── auth.ts          # BetterAuth configuration
│   ├── db.ts            # Drizzle database setup
│   ├── utils.ts         # Utility functions
│   └── validations.ts   # Zod schemas
├── hooks/               # Custom React hooks
├── store/              # Zustand stores
├── types/              # TypeScript type definitions
└── data/              # Static data and constants
```

## 🔧 TypeScript Standards (5.8)

### Configuration
- Use strictest possible TypeScript config
- Enable all strict flags
- Use `--erasableSyntaxOnly` for performance
- Prefer `satisfies` operator over type assertions
- Always define return types for functions

### Type Safety Rules
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Explicit return types
function calculateFare(distance: number): Promise<FareResult> {
  return fareService.calculate(distance)
}

// ❌ BAD: Implicit any
function calculateFare(distance) {
  return fareService.calculate(distance)
}

// ✅ GOOD: Use satisfies operator
const config = {
  apiUrl: process.env.API_URL,
  timeout: 5000
} satisfies ApiConfig

// ✅ GOOD: Branded types for IDs
type StationId = string & { readonly brand: unique symbol }
type UserId = string & { readonly brand: unique symbol }
```

### Import/Export Standards
- Use named exports, avoid default exports except for pages/layouts
- Group imports: external → internal → relative
- Use type-only imports when possible

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Organized imports
import type { NextPage } from 'next'
import { Suspense } from 'react'

import type { Station } from '@/types/station'
import { StationCard } from '@/components/custom/station-card'
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'

import './styles.css'
```

## ⚛️ React 19 & Component Standards

### Component Architecture
- Prefer function components with hooks
- Use React.memo() sparingly, only for expensive renders
- Leverage React 19 Compiler optimizations
- Use Server Components by default, Client Components when needed

### Component Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Server Component with proper typing
interface StationListProps {
  stations: Station[]
  searchQuery?: string
}

export async function StationList({ stations, searchQuery }: StationListProps) {
  const filteredStations = stations.filter(/* filtering logic */)
  
  return (
    <div className="grid gap-4">
      {filteredStations.map(station => (
        <StationCard key={station.id} station={station} />
      ))}
    </div>
  )
}

// ✅ GOOD: Client Component with hooks
'use client'

interface SearchBarProps {
  onSearch: (query: string) => void
  placeholder?: string
}

export function SearchBar({ onSearch, placeholder = "Search stations..." }: SearchBarProps) {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('')
  
  return (
    <input
      type="text"
      value={query}
      onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)}
      onKeyDown={(e) => e.key === 'Enter' && onSearch(query)}
      placeholder={placeholder}
      className="w-full px-4 py-2 border rounded-lg"
    />
  )
}
```

### Hooks Standards
- Custom hooks must start with 'use'
- Keep hooks focused and single-purpose
- Use Zustand for client state, TanStack Query for server state
- Prefer useShallow from Zustand for performance

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Focused custom hook
function useStationSearch(initialQuery = '') {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState(initialQuery)
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false)
  
  const { data: stations } = useQuery({
    queryKey: ['stations', query],
    queryFn: () => searchStations(query),
    enabled: query.length > 2
  })
  
  return { query, setQuery, stations, isLoading }
}
```

## 🎨 UI & Styling Standards

### Tailwind CSS v4 (Oxide Engine)
- Use CSS-first approach, avoid configuration
- Prefer utility classes over custom CSS
- Use design tokens consistently
- Implement proper responsive design

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Semantic utility classes
<div className="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
  <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">
    Find Your Metro Station
  </h1>
  <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
    {/* Content */}
  </div>
</div>

// ❌ BAD: Inline styles or complex custom CSS
<div style={{ padding: '32px', margin: '16px auto' }}>
```

### Shadcn/ui & OriginUI Integration
- Always extend Shadcn components, don't modify source
- Use OriginUI for advanced patterns
- Maintain consistent design tokens
- Follow accessibility guidelines (WCAG 2.1 AA)

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Extending Shadcn components
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'

interface StationButtonProps extends React.ComponentProps<typeof Button> {
  station: Station
  isSelected?: boolean
}

export function StationButton({ 
  station, 
  isSelected, 
  className, 
  ...props 
}: StationButtonProps) {
  return (
    <Button
      variant={isSelected ? 'default' : 'outline'}
      className={cn(
        'w-full justify-start text-left',
        isSelected && 'ring-2 ring-primary',
        className
      )}
      {...props}
    >
      <MapPin className="mr-2 h-4 w-4" />
      {station.name}
    </Button>
  )
}
```

### Animation Standards
- Use Framer Motion for complex animations
- Prefer CSS animations for simple transitions
- Respect user's motion preferences
- Keep animations under 300ms for micro-interactions

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Framer Motion with accessibility
import { motion } from 'framer-motion'

export function StationCard({ station }: { station: Station }) {
  return (
    <motion.div
      initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 20 }}
      animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
      transition={{ duration: 0.2 }}
      className="p-4 border rounded-lg hover:shadow-md transition-shadow"
    >
      {/* Content */}
    </motion.div>
  )
}
```

## 🗃️ Data & State Management

### Drizzle ORM Standards
- Define schemas in separate files
- Use proper TypeScript types
- Implement proper relationships
- Use prepared statements for performance

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Drizzle schema definition
import { pgTable, text, timestamp, decimal, boolean } from 'drizzle-orm/pg-core'

export const stations = pgTable('stations', {
  id: text('id').primaryKey(),
  name: text('name').notNull(),
  line: text('line').notNull(),
  latitude: decimal('latitude', { precision: 10, scale: 7 }).notNull(),
  longitude: decimal('longitude', { precision: 10, scale: 7 }).notNull(),
  isActive: boolean('is_active').default(true),
  createdAt: timestamp('created_at').defaultNow(),
  updatedAt: timestamp('updated_at').defaultNow()
})

export type Station = typeof stations.$inferSelect
export type NewStation = typeof stations.$inferInsert
```

### Zod v4 Validation
- Create reusable schemas
- Use proper error messages
- Implement client and server validation
- Leverage JSON Schema generation

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Zod validation schemas
import { z } from 'zod'

export const StationSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().min(1, 'Station ID is required'),
  name: z.string().min(2, 'Station name must be at least 2 characters'),
  line: z.enum(['RED', 'GREEN', 'BLUE'], {
    errorMap: () => ({ message: 'Invalid metro line' })
  }),
  latitude: z.number().min(-90).max(90),
  longitude: z.number().min(-180).max(180),
  isActive: z.boolean().default(true)
})

export const SearchParamsSchema = z.object({
  query: z.string().optional(),
  line: z.string().optional(),
  page: z.coerce.number().min(1).default(1)
})

export type StationInput = z.infer<typeof StationSchema>
export type SearchParams = z.infer<typeof SearchParamsSchema>
```

### Zustand v5 Store Standards
- Keep stores focused and domain-specific
- Use useShallow for performance
- Implement proper TypeScript types
- Use immer for complex state updates

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Zustand store with TypeScript
import { create } from 'zustand'
import { immer } from 'zustand/middleware/immer'

interface UserPreferencesState {
  favoriteStations: string[]
  searchHistory: SearchHistoryItem[]
  darkMode: boolean
  actions: {
    addFavorite: (stationId: string) => void
    removeFavorite: (stationId: string) => void
    addToHistory: (search: SearchHistoryItem) => void
    toggleDarkMode: () => void
  }
}

export const useUserPreferences = create<UserPreferencesState>()(
  immer((set) => ({
    favoriteStations: [],
    searchHistory: [],
    darkMode: false,
    actions: {
      addFavorite: (stationId) =>
        set((state) => {
          if (!state.favoriteStations.includes(stationId)) {
            state.favoriteStations.push(stationId)
          }
        }),
      // ... other actions
    }
  }))
)
```

### TanStack Query Standards
- Use proper query keys
- Implement error boundaries
- Use optimistic updates for mutations
- Leverage Suspense for loading states

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: TanStack Query with proper patterns
import { useQuery, useMutation, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'

export function useStations(searchParams: SearchParams) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['stations', searchParams],
    queryFn: () => fetchStations(searchParams),
    staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // 5 minutes
    gcTime: 10 * 60 * 1000, // 10 minutes
  })
}

export function useAddToFavorites() {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient()
  
  return useMutation({
    mutationFn: addStationToFavorites,
    onMutate: async (stationId) => {
      await queryClient.cancelQueries({ queryKey: ['favorites'] })
      
      const previousFavorites = queryClient.getQueryData(['favorites'])
      
      queryClient.setQueryData(['favorites'], (old: string[]) => [
        ...(old || []),
        stationId
      ])
      
      return { previousFavorites }
    },
    onError: (err, stationId, context) => {
      queryClient.setQueryData(['favorites'], context?.previousFavorites)
    },
    onSettled: () => {
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['favorites'] })
    }
  })
}
```

## 🔐 Authentication & Security

### BetterAuth Integration
- Use proper session management
- Implement CSRF protection
- Use secure cookie settings
- Follow OAuth best practices

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: BetterAuth configuration
import { betterAuth } from 'better-auth'
import { drizzleAdapter } from 'better-auth/adapters/drizzle'

export const auth = betterAuth({
  database: drizzleAdapter(db, {
    provider: 'pg'
  }),
  emailAndPassword: {
    enabled: true,
    requireEmailVerification: true
  },
  socialProviders: {
    google: {
      clientId: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID!,
      clientSecret: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET!
    }
  },
  session: {
    expiresIn: 60 * 60 * 24 * 7, // 1 week
    updateAge: 60 * 60 * 24 // 1 day
  }
})
```

## 🗺️ Maps & Location Standards

### MapLibre GL JS
- Use vector tiles for performance
- Implement proper error handling
- Use Web Workers for heavy computations
- Optimize for mobile devices

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: MapLibre implementation
import maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css'

export function useMapLibre(containerRef: RefObject<HTMLDivElement>) {
  const [map, setMap] = useState<maplibregl.Map | null>(null)
  
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!containerRef.current) return
    
    const mapInstance = new maplibregl.Map({
      container: containerRef.current,
      style: 'https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets/style.json?key=' + process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_KEY,
      center: [90.4125, 23.8103], // Dhaka coordinates
      zoom: 12,
      attributionControl: false
    })
    
    mapInstance.on('load', () => {
      setMap(mapInstance)
    })
    
    return () => mapInstance.remove()
  }, [])
  
  return map
}
```

