## 🚫 Things to Avoid

### Performance Killers
- ❌ Large bundle sizes (keep chunks under 50KB)
- ❌ Blocking operations in main thread
- ❌ Memory leaks from event listeners
- ❌ Excessive re-renders

### Anti-Patterns
- ❌ Prop drilling (use context or state management)
- ❌ Inline object/function creation in render
- ❌ Direct DOM manipulation
- ❌ Ignoring accessibility

### Security Issues
- ❌ Client-side secrets
- ❌ Unvalidated user input
- ❌ Insecure authentication flows
- ❌ XSS vulnerabilities

## 🎯 Success Metrics

### Performance Targets
- First Contentful Paint: < 1.2s
- Largest Contentful Paint: < 2.5s
- Cumulative Layout Shift: < 0.1
- First Input Delay: < 100ms

### Quality Targets
- TypeScript strict mode: 100%
- Test coverage: > 80%
- Accessibility score: 100 (Lighthouse)
- Bundle size: < 200KB initial load

---

**Remember**: These rules are guidelines to achieve blazing fast, modern, and maintainable code. Always prioritize user experience and code clarity over premature optimization.